WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.180
- I was just hard core
GameStop, GME, 100%.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.487
We're going to the moon.

00:00:05.487 --> 00:00:08.090
- [Narrator] The GameStop frenzy
brought many new investors

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:09.353
into the market.

00:00:09.353 --> 00:00:10.578
- I just start pounding away

00:00:10.578 --> 00:00:12.070
and just like okay, buy, buy, buy

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.434
and it keeps going up and up and up.

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.750
And so I'm getting excited.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.670
- [Narrator] Nearly seven
million people downloaded

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:19.370
the eight most popular trading apps,

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.540
including Robinhood in January.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.690
That's more than double
the previous month.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.920
But this community of
online investors existed

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.640
before GME took off.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.870
It's been growing throughout the pandemic

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:33.260
and it lives on social media.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.480
- Robinhood users have
been going crazy for Hertz.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.800
- Here you go, NASDAQ versus
NYSE, new highs today.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.350
- That break yesterday
gave you a monster winner.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.090
- [Narrator] YouTube
channels, Reddit forums,

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:45.980
Facebook groups, Discord chats

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.650
and TikTok influencers like Taylor Price

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:50.600
are all talking trades.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.900
- This community is meme culture,

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.960
it's Gen Z, it's Millennial

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.610
and it's people who don't
want to work the nine-to-five.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:01.610
The reason I am able to trade full time

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:05.050
is solely because of the Discord group.

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:07.670
- [HaiKhuu] I got SM Energy at 214.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:09.360
- [Narrator] So who's a part
of this growing community

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.900
of traders seeking and
sharing investment information

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:13.230
on social media?

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:16.890
And how are the communities
helping them chase the market?

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:17.920
- Hello, my name is Collin Chung.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.580
I'm 33 years old.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.700
I'm CEO of Omni Group Consulting

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.350
and I'm new to the investing market.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:27.910
- [Narrator] Collin Chung
started trading on January 25th

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:30.310
as hype around GameStop was spreading

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:32.600
and the company stock was gaining.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:35.160
- That morning, I throw in maybe $500

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.140
and it turned into $800.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.520
- [Narrator] And as the share
price climbed the next day,

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.840
Chung continued to invest.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.840
- I was able to somehow get a
few thousand dollars in there.

00:01:47.455 --> 00:01:51.103
I wake up the next morning and it doubles.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:54.130
But it was at that point

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:58.500
that I realized it's
very much like gambling.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:01:59.970
- [Narrator] Chung has
a business background

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.420
but not in investment.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:02.940
So for his stock decisions,

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.890
he turns to social media.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.190
- I wanna talk to you guys about GameStop.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:10.310
- Why is GME, AMC still
down? Will it go back up?

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:11.610
- All the ones that I used to use,

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.270
LinkedIn, Facebook, not so much.

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:16.113
I'm looking at very much
more real-time functionality.

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:20.360
Twitter, Instagram, TikTok.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.740
- Is this a short squeeze?

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:24.290
- [Narrator] And of course,
he's watching the market.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:25.970
- [Collin] So this is
my triple monitor setup.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:30.190
This is primarily where I'm
monitoring the stock market

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.340
for the specific stocks that I'm watching.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.270
- [Narrator] Despite the setup,

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:35.900
Chung isn't considering
making trading his career.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:38.680
- I look at it like I'm spending $3,000

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:43.220
to entertain myself to
see if I can make it grow.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:45.520
- [Narrator] That why Chung
says after taking out most

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.940
of what he needed to cover
his initial investment,

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:51.030
he's put the rest of his
returns back in the market.

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.670
And he's still holding GameStop,

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:55.240
an investment that's now costing him.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:58.420
- If there's a profit and
payoff at the end, great.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:03.230
If not, I just wanna
have a vested interest

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:04.510
in seeing where this goes

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:07.473
'cause I think that the
results are gonna be important.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.440
- Here's three reasons why small stocks

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:11.913
may have big potential.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.380
- 20-year-old TikTok
influencer Taylor Price

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:18.060
also saw gains during the GME frenzy.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.510
Her follower count hit one million

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.920
but not because she was
buying into the meme stock.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:26.810
- I wasn't saying oh,
oh, look at the situation

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:27.980
as a buying opportunity.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:30.460
I was looking at it as
a learning opportunity.

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:32.930
I just made 350,000 on GameStop.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:33.840
What?

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.930
No way, what are you gonna do with it?

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.390
The first thing that I'm going to do

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:40.830
is set aside 40% for taxes.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:42.340
- [Narrator] Her posts
are quick and informative,

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.370
seeking to explain basic financial terms

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.100
and show her followers
how to make the most

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.060
of their money.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:50.110
- Your budget truly depends
on your personal lifestyle.

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:53.100
75% of my audience is female

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.230
and you don't especially see them

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:57.150
being so young like myself.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:04:00.090
They want to start
controlling their own finances

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:01.830
when maybe in the past,

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:04.600
their father or their older guardian

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.820
that was male had done so.

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:07.797
- [Narrator] But Price didn't set out

00:04:07.797 --> 00:04:09.960
to be a social media influencer.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:11.530
She first got interested in finance,

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:13.530
taking college courses on the subject.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.050
And she said she started investing

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:18.041
because she saw how much
money others were making.

00:04:18.041 --> 00:04:19.110
- This is how bad the market did today.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:22.220
And this is how good I did today.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:23.870
Right here, people.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:25.270
- [Narrator] For many of her successes,

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.770
she says she also had a lot of busts

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:29.930
and realized that she
needed to take a step back

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.760
to learn some personal
finance fundamentals.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:35.130
- When I had this awakening moment

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:36.400
about financial literacy

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:37.890
and what school wasn't teaching us,

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:41.420
that is when I said I
need to take this online.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:43.340
There things nobody told
you about before investing

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.430
in the stock market.

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:46.510
- [Narrator] Price still actively invests.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:48.040
She says social media is good

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.700
for qualitative analysis

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.410
but should be followed by research

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:52.940
and her posts aim to show that.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:55.290
- Social media should be acting

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:58.330
as not just giving somebody a fish

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:01.360
but teaching people how to fish.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.264
What? This is crazy, thank you, Taylor.

00:05:03.264 --> 00:05:05.430
- Hi, I'm John Bevis

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:08.020
and I am 28 years old

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:10.630
and I am a full-time stock trader.

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:12.950
- [Narrator] John Bevis, who
once held GameStop shares,

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:16.930
which he sold before the spike
said his goal is consistency.

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:19.810
He wants a monthly paycheck,
not a one-time bonus.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.550
- Consistent trading to me

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:26.550
is able to continuously make your return

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.750
without risking too much money

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:33.810
and always limiting your loss.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:35.790
- [Narrator] He says
consistency is a goal shared

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:38.410
by members of a paid
Discord chat he's a part of.

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:40.610
The group, run by a company called HaiKhuu

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:42.890
has roughly 22,000 participants

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:45.770
and includes both a text
chat and voice call.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:49.930
- [HaiKhuu] Yeah, I got SM
Energy at 214 and now it's at 12

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:52.091
but I sold off at like 11.

00:05:52.091 --> 00:05:54.590
- Well, the Discord group has benefited me

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:57.820
in almost a way a can't explain

00:05:57.820 --> 00:05:59.550
because of the amount of knowledge

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:02.510
and effort and support they
put towards their members.

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:03.970
- [Narrator] Bevis
started trading full time

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:05.370
about a year and a half ago,

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:06.840
leaving his job in construction,

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.160
which paid him $45 an hour.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.790
So far, trading isn't
paying him quite as well.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:13.850
He says he's bringing in anywhere from 800

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.900
to $2,000 per month

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:18.070
but he says that's enough for now.

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:22.620
- I'm not taking large
vacations or anything like that.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:24.750
I can travel if I want to

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.630
but that will take time
away from me here trading

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:29.080
and that's what I love to do.

